    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The cited bullet [ev-e2c282154595] is just a metric name, but it sits in a list that the section intro [ev-1f419676f177] introduces with \"These metrics will be changed\". That intro says the change concretely: in 3.0.0, metrics with the `cortex_` prefix now start with `loki_` because `metrics_namespace` defaults to `loki`. Operators can keep the old prefix by setting `metrics_namespace` to `cortex`, but that setting is deprecated and will be removed in the next minor release. So an engineer could write the assertion: the subject is the metric `cortex_prometheus_rule_group_last_duration_seconds`, the change is a rename to `loki_prometheus_rule_group_last_duration_seconds`, exposed environments are those that leave `metrics_namespace` at its default, and in those environments the old metric name is no longer emitted.",
